DDXPlus: A New Dataset For Automatic Medical Diagnosis (NeurIPS 2022).
Dataset authors: Arsene Fansi Tchango, Rishab Goel, Zhi Wen, Julien Martel, Joumana Ghosn.
Official project: https://mila-iqia.github.io/ddxplus/
Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.09148
English data pinned to Figshare article 22687585, version 2:
https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/DDXPlus_Dataset_English_/22687585/2
Data license: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Adaptation: selected source CSV rows are converted to JSONL; evidence queries are
bounded to 15 distinct follow-up questions and expose static released observations.
Recipe v2 optionally restricts selection and the actor catalog to a fixed six-condition
curriculum. The first canonical diagnosis receives exact pathology accuracy independently
of secondary differential validity. Full49 source metadata is preserved.
This adaptation is not an official DDXPlus evaluation protocol or a clinical system.
No medical correctness, clinical validity, safety or deployment fitness is claimed.
Patients are synthetic, generated from a proprietary knowledge base and commercial
rule-based ASD system, not de-identified records of real patients.
